{"type": "mcq", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"x squared plus y squared equals 36\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>36</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"y equals m x plus StartFraction b Over 4 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mi>m</mi>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mfrac>\n\t\t\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t\t\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t\t</mfrac>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the given system of equations, <math alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> are negative constants. In the <em>xy</em>-plane, the graphs of the equations in the given system intersect at the point <math alttext=\"left parenthesis negative 5 comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, where <math alttext=\"y less than 0\"><mi>y</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Which expression represents the value of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>?</p>", "keys": ["4143b2b9-0071-4bf7-9d30-3b5bb7e4cea1"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "cc840e36-dae5-4477-b142-bbd10c37f49a", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"minus StartFraction 5 m Over 4 EndFraction plus StartFraction StartRoot 11 EndRoot Over 4 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mfrac>\n\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t\t\t\t<mi>m</mi>\n\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t</mfrac>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mfrac>\n\t\t\t<msqrt>\n\t\t\t\t<mn>11</mn>\n\t\t\t</msqrt>\n\t\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t</mfrac>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "8de9a653-a890-426b-ba3a-602c8b6fa6bf", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 5 m Over 4 EndFraction minus StartFraction StartRoot 11 EndRoot Over 4 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mfrac>\n\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t\t\t\t<mi>m</mi>\n\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t</mfrac>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mfrac>\n\t\t\t<msqrt>\n\t\t\t\t<mn>11</mn>\n\t\t\t</msqrt>\n\t\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t</mfrac>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "8b1eca69-902c-40c7-9230-74bee5dcc934", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"minus 20 m plus 4 StartRoot 11 EndRoot\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>20</mn>\n\t\t<mi>m</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t<msqrt>\n\t\t\t<mn>11</mn>\n\t\t</msqrt>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "4143b2b9-0071-4bf7-9d30-3b5bb7e4cea1", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"20 m minus 4 StartRoot 11 EndRoot\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>20</mn>\n\t\t<mi>m</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t<msqrt>\n\t\t\t<mn>11</mn>\n\t\t</msqrt>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the graphs of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x squared plus y squared equals 36\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals m x plus StartFraction b Over 4 EndFraction\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> are negative constants, intersect at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis negative 5 comma y right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo></math> in the <em>x</em><em>y</em>-plane. It follows that this intersection point represents a solution to the given system of equations. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 5\"><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> in the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x squared plus y squared equals 36\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis negative 5 right parenthesis squared plus y squared equals 36\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"25 plus y squared equals 36\"><mn>25</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"25\"><mn>25</mn></math> from each side of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y squared equals 11\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></math>. It's also given that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y less than 0\"><mi>y</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, so taking the negative square root of each side of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals minus StartRoot 11 EndRoot\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>11</mn></msqrt></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 5\"><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"minus StartRoot 11 EndRoot\"><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>11</mn></msqrt></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math> in the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals m x plus StartFraction b Over 4 EndFraction\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"minus StartRoot 11 EndRoot equals m left parenthesis negative 5 right parenthesis plus StartFraction b Over 4 EndFraction\"><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>11</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"minus StartRoot 11 EndRoot equals minus 5 m plus StartFraction b Over 4 EndFraction\"><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>11</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. Adding <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 m\"><mn>5</mn><mi>m</mi></math> to each side of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 m minus StartRoot 11 EndRoot equals StartFraction b Over 4 EndFraction\"><mn>5</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>11</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4 left parenthesis 5 m minus StartRoot 11 EndRoot right parenthesis equals b\"><mn>4</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>11</mn></msqrt><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></math>. Applying the distributive property to the left-hand side of this equation yields&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"20 m minus 4 StartRoot 11 EndRoot equals b\"><mn>20</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>11</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></math>. Therefore, the expression&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"20 m minus 4 StartRoot 11 EndRoot\"><mn>20</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>11</mn></msqrt></math> represents the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect&nbsp;and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>", "externalid": "207c18b2-0202-4869-bc5f-64c10fac4239", "correct_answer": ["D"]}